UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKER
Thank

[[00:00:00.650]]
SPEAKER 1 (LOWER-PITCHED VOICE)
you, Chairman Engel. I rise in strong support of this resolution, sponsored by my good friend from Michigan, Congresswoman Slotkin. The Trump administration's foreign policy failures have brought us to the brink of war. The administration has provided no evidence to demonstrate what imminent threat made Qasem Soleimani's assassination and the perilous, predictable fallout necessary.

[[00:00:28.820]]
UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKER
but

[[00:00:29.200]]
SPEAKER 1 (LOWER-PITCHED VOICE)
they have demonstrated a shocking dismissiveness as to what's at stake. On the threat of retaliation from Iran, Secretary Pompeo said, "It may be that there's a little noise here in the interim." President Trump said, "If it happens, it happens."

[[00:00:46.700]]
UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKER
To the

[[00:00:47.240]]
SPEAKER 1 (LOWER-PITCHED VOICE)
parents who are worried sick about their kids serving in the Middle East, it isn't a little noise. Their children's lives are at stake.

[[00:00:58.180]]
UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKER
Those

[[00:00:58.600]]
SPEAKER 1 (LOWER-PITCHED VOICE)
stakes make today's vote necessary. The question before us is simple. Can we let this president drag us into another war that will cost billions of taxpayer dollars and, most importantly, American lives? Will we at long last stand up and fulfill our constitutional duty to make decisions on war and peace? I urge my colleagues to vote for this resolution and I yield back the balance of my time.
